# JVM options of the tests (surefire argLine = @src/test/surefire-jvm.args). The legacy goldens were recorded under zone UTC, locale en-US,
# UTF-8 files and LF as System.lineSeparator() (the legacy ran on Linux). A Java argument file is the only way to pass a line feed:
# inside the quotes the launcher reads \n as LF.
-Duser.timezone=UTC
-Dfile.encoding=UTF-8
-Duser.language=en
-Duser.country=US
"-Dline.separator=\n"
